==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Great Angel Chibinel]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Ancient Magamojoe]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**3 [[Formicidaean Ariant]]s spawn, delay 43.33~50 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,500f</sup>.
**3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**1 [[Cumulus Gallus]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
**1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns.
**1 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Avoid using most Surge units in this stage, as the majority of all enemies will simply dismiss them.

Ancient Magamojoe is the primary threat here, since he has devastating attacks and a massive 2,200,000 health. Attempt to kill him as fast as possible; his 50% Surge chance can cause you to lose if it procs too often, so don't be surprised if you have to try again... not to mention he's knockback and slow immune, making [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] ineffective. A good counter is [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Luza]]; while it doesn't require Epic Behemoth Stones and performs well versus the Behemoths here, it is expensive to evolve, and it is only obtainable after completing [[Revival of Origin]]. There is value in completing either stage first, whether it is best to get Luza first or the other Uncanny Legends True Forms depends by the player.

As soon as you obtain the necessary amount of Epic Behemoth Stones, evolve the most helpful Uncanny Legend units as their newly acquired Behemoth Slayer abilities can be put to good use here. [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] is recommended as its anti-Relic ability makes it an excellent counter against Magamojoe, while [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]] is an excellent generalist. [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] and [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] are far less effective, so it's recommended to invest in them later, when you can consistently clear this stage. If you are truly desperate (without the necessary ubers) and have lots of cat food to spare, the ultimate last resort option is the fact that this stage lacks [[No Continues]]. Once you manage to secure Naala, you won't be ever needing to spend as much cat food on the rest.

=== '''Recommended Units''' ===

* [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] - Having very high health and Behemoth Slayer with a massive unit-specific 50% dodge, Cat Egg Pod can tank a gargantuan amount of attacks from the Behemoths here and easily stall, though getting this unit is another challenge in itself.
* [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Although Courier Cat doesn't fare as well against the nasty Behemoths, his Massive Damage to Red and Behemoth Slayer still work here to quickly eliminate [[Casaurian Ahirujo]].

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: She makes light work of the Magamojoe. Provided you are meatshielding properly, she also acts as a good generalist attacker, so you shouldn't just view her as the "Magamojoe Killer".
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Players who have acquired this unit's Ultra Form can use him as an effective source of support. While he doesn't target anything beyond Chibinel, he can provide significant amounts of damage at extreme range, far beyond the reach of most threats, not to mention his far-reaching Wave Attack, as only [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] is Wave Immune.
*[[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventurer Kanna]] - With extreme coverage through her Long Distance attacks, Massive Damage to Darks and Behemoth Slayer, Kanna can whittle down Darkjo quickly and inflict reasonable damage to the Behemoths, even if they dismiss her Surges.

